"splitting **after** construction, and without a setter that line would "
"stop working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring of pdf_extract.ExtractTextPdfBlockOrFailPage:3
msgid ""
"The only pipe of this module also exposed directly among the utilities, "
"because author modules use it for blocks that are none of the three "
"standard cases below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.utils.pdf_extract.PdfLineSelection:3 of
msgid ""
"It wraps the *relative* form rather than the either-or one, because the "
"relative branch is a superset of the absolute one — an absolute selection"
" is an absolute leaf inside a relative tree — and keeping only one makes "
"the operators definable once instead of over four combinations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring
#: freeports.utils.pdf_extract.PdfLineSelection.area_from_bounds:1 of
msgid ""
"Each edge is either a number, an absolute coordinate, **or** another "
"selection, whose corresponding edge is taken. The form a formats "
"repository uses most after matching by text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.utils.pdf_extract.PdfLineSelection.contextualize:1
#: of
msgid "The selection resolved against a set of lines, without applying it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.utils.pdf_extract.PdfLineSelection.select:1 of
msgid "The lines satisfying the selection, in the order they appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.utils.pdf_extract.PdfLineSelection.select:3 of
msgid ""
"The selection is *contextualised* first: its relative parts need the "
"page's lines to know what they refer to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.utils.pdf_extract.TableConfig:3 of
msgid ""
"The rows and columns accept a single configuration or an iterable: "
"passing one directly is the form a formats repository uses most often."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring freeports.utils.pdf_extract.TablePosAlgorithm:3 of
msgid ""
"Not a catalogue of names like the block-type ones: these flags "
"**combine** with `|`, and that is how a formats repository writes them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docstring
#: freeports.utils.pdf_extract.TablePosAlgorithm.from_expression:1 of
